IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `ei1-payment`
IMPORT `ei1-benefit-period`

-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Part I, "Special Benefits": s 23 (parental benefits). Layer 1 of piece ei1.
-- Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30.
-- Imports ei1-payment (s 12(3)) and ei1-benefit-period (the helpers of s 10(13) and s 10(15) that s 23(3.2) repeats).
-- "Reduced or eliminated as prescribed" (s 23(3.5)): the Regulations deposited prescribe a reduction where provincial
-- benefits are paid under a provincial plan (regs 76.16 and 76.17, piece er4); the amount is an input.

§ `Section 23(1) to (1.3) - who may claim, and the election`

-- src:509 | 23 (1) Despite section 18, but subject to this section, benefits are payable to a major attachment claimant to care for one or more new-born children of the claimant or one or more children placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption under the laws governing adoption in the province in which the claimant resides.
-- "Under the laws governing adoption in the province in which the claimant resides" qualifies the children placed for adoption.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(1) (src:509)
GIVEN `the claimant is a major attachment claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are to care for one or more new-born children of the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits are to care for one or more children placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption under the laws governing adoption in the province in which the claimant resides` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(1) benefits are payable to the claimant to care for one or more new-born or adopted children` IF
        `the claimant is a major attachment claimant`
    AND (   `the benefits are to care for one or more new-born children of the claimant`
         OR `the benefits are to care for one or more children placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption under the laws governing adoption in the province in which the claimant resides`)

-- src:511 | (1.1) In a claim for benefits made under this section, a claimant shall elect the maximum number of weeks referred to in either subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) or (ii) for which benefits may be paid.
-- The claimant "shall elect" the 35 or the 61 weeks; the election is an input, and the weeks it gives are those of
-- subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) or (ii).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(1.1) (src:511)
GIVEN election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(1.1) the maximum number of weeks elected` IS
    fromMaybe 0 (`s 12(3) the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid in a benefit period for the reason` `caring for a new-born or adopted child` election)

-- src:513 | (1.2) The election is irrevocable once benefits are paid under this section or under section 152.05 in respect of the same child or children.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(1.2) (src:513)
GIVEN `benefits have been paid under section 23 or under section 152.05 in respect of the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(1.2) the election is irrevocable` IF
    `benefits have been paid under section 23 or under section 152.05 in respect of the same child or children`

-- src:515 | (1.3) If two major attachment claimants each make a claim for benefits under this section — or one major attachment claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and an individual makes a claim for benefits under section 152.05 — in respect of the same child or children, the election made under subsection (1.1) or 152.05(1.1) by the first claimant or individual, as the case may be, to make a claim for benefits under this section or under section 152.05 is binding on both claimants or on the claimant and the individual.
-- Where two claims are made in respect of the same child or children (two major attachment claimants, or one and an
-- individual under section 152.05), the election of the first to claim is binding on both.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(1.3) (src:515)
GIVEN `the claimant's own election` IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the election of the first claimant or individual to make a claim under section 23 or 152.05 in respect of the same child or children, if another has made one` IS A MAYBE `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH AN `Election of maximum weeks`
DECIDE `s 23(1.3) the election that binds the claimant` IS
    CONSIDER `the election of the first claimant or individual to make a claim under section 23 or 152.05 in respect of the same child or children, if another has made one`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the claimant's own election`
    WHEN JUST first THEN first

§ `Section 23(2) to (3.4) - the period during which benefits are payable`

-- src:517 | (2) Subject to section 12, benefits under this section are payable for each week of unemployment in the period
-- src:518 | (a) that begins with the week in which the child or children of the claimant are born or the child or children are actually placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption; and
-- src:519 | (b) that ends 52 weeks after the week in which the child or children of the claimant are born or the child or children are actually placed with the claimant for the purpose of adoption.
-- The week of birth or placement is taken as the week the period begins with, and the period ends on the last day of the
-- week 52 weeks after it (the same reading as s 22(2): fork F-22-2 in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(2) (src:517-519)
GIVEN `a day in the week in which the child or children are born or actually placed with the claimant` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Period of days`
DECIDE `s 23(2) the period during which benefits are payable` IS
    `Period of days` OF (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `a day in the week in which the child or children are born or actually placed with the claimant`),
                        (`s 2(1) the Saturday that ends the week containing` (`s 2(1) the Sunday that begins the week containing` `a day in the week in which the child or children are born or actually placed with the claimant` PLUS `weeks as days` 52))

-- src:521 | (3) If the child or children referred to in subsection (1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection (2), the period is extended by the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3) (src:521)
GIVEN `the child or children referred to in subsection (1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(3) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because the children are in hospital` IS
    IF `the child or children referred to in subsection (1) are hospitalized during the period referred to in subsection (2)`
    THEN `the number of weeks during which the child or children are hospitalized`
    ELSE 0

-- src:523 | (3.01) If, during the period referred to in subsection (2), the start date of a claimant’s period of parental leave is deferred or a claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act, the period is extended by the number of weeks during which the claimant’s parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty, as the case may be.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3.01) (src:523)
GIVEN `during the period referred to in subsection (2), the start date of the claimant's period of parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks during which the claimant's parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(3.01) the number of weeks by which the period is extended because of the Canadian Forces` IS
    IF `during the period referred to in subsection (2), the start date of the claimant's period of parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty from parental leave, in accordance with regulations made under the National Defence Act`
    THEN `the number of weeks during which the claimant's parental leave is deferred or the claimant is directed to return to duty`
    ELSE 0

-- src:525 | (3.1) No extension under subsection (3) or (3.01) may result in the period being longer than 104 weeks.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3.1) (src:525)
`s 23(3.1) the longest the period may be after an extension under subsection (3) or (3.01), in weeks` MEANS 104

-- src:527 | (3.2) The period referred to in subsection (2) is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks referred to in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) or (ii) if, during a claimant’s benefit period,
-- src:528 | (a) regular benefits were not paid to the claimant;
-- src:529 | (b) benefits were paid to the claimant for more than one of the reasons mentioned in paragraphs 12(3)(a) to (f);
-- src:530 | (c) the maximum total number of weeks established for those reasons is greater than 50; and
-- src:531 | (d) benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) but for fewer than the applicable maximum number of weeks established for that reason.
-- The conditions repeat those of s 10(13) with one more, (d): benefits were paid for the reason in paragraph 12(3)(b) but
-- for fewer than the applicable maximum. The text does not say how many weeks the period is extended by "so that benefits
-- may be paid up to the applicable maximum"; it is read as the extension of s 10(13), that is, to the length of s 10(15)
-- (fork F-23-3.2 in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3.2) (src:527-531)
GIVEN `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(3.2) the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` IF
        NOT (`regular benefits were paid to the claimant`)
    AND count (`ei1 the special benefits actually paid` paid) AT LEAST 2
    AND `s 10(13)(c) the maximum total number of weeks established for the reasons for which special benefits were paid` paid election GREATER THAN 50
    AND any (GIVEN p YIELD p's `ei1 the reason for which special benefits were paid` EQUALS `caring for a new-born or adopted child`
                       AND p's `ei1 the number of weeks for which special benefits were paid for it` BELOW `s 10(13) the maximum number of weeks established for the reason for which special benefits were paid` p election)
            (`ei1 the special benefits actually paid` paid)

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3.2) (src:527-531)
GIVEN `the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks` IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A LIST OF `ei1 Special benefits paid for one reason`
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(3.2) the number of weeks by which the period is extended` IS
    IF `the period is extended so that benefits may be paid up to the applicable maximum number of weeks`
    THEN max 0 (`s 10(15) the maximum number of weeks in a benefit period extended under subsection (13)` paid election MINUS `s 10(2) the length of a benefit period in weeks, before any extension`)
    ELSE 0

-- src:533 | (3.21) The period referred to in subsection (2) is extended by 26 weeks so that benefits may be paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) up to the maximum number of weeks if, during a claimant’s benefit period,
-- src:534 | (a) benefits were paid to the claimant for that reason and the applicable maximum number of weeks is established in subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii);
-- src:535 | (b) regular benefits were not paid to the claimant; and
-- src:536 | (c) benefits were not paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3.21) (src:533-536)
GIVEN `benefits were paid to the claimant for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(3.21) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` IS
    IF     `benefits were paid to the claimant for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)`
       AND election EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
       AND NOT (`regular benefits were paid to the claimant`)
       AND NOT (`benefits were paid for any reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(a), (c), (d), (e) or (f)`)
    THEN 26
    ELSE 0

-- src:538 | (3.22) If, during a claimant’s benefit period, regular benefits were paid, benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b) in the case where the applicable maximum number of weeks is established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii), and benefits were paid for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6) as determined under subsection 12(7), the period referred to in subsection (2) is extended for the same number of weeks as the extension established under subsection 10(13.02).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3.22) (src:538)
GIVEN `regular benefits were paid to the claimant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `benefits were paid for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6) as determined under subsection 12(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of weeks of the extension established under subsection 10(13.02)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(3.22) the number of weeks by which the period is extended for regular and special benefits` IS
    IF     `regular benefits were paid to the claimant`
       AND `benefits were paid for the reason mentioned in paragraph 12(3)(b)`
       AND election EQUALS `the 61-week maximum`
       AND `benefits were paid for fewer than the total number of weeks established under subsection 12(6) as determined under subsection 12(7)`
    THEN `the number of weeks of the extension established under subsection 10(13.02)`
    ELSE 0

-- s 23(3.23): [Repealed, 2012, c. 27, s. 17] (src line 539). Nothing to encode.

-- src:541 | (3.3) An extension under subsection (3.2) must not result in the period referred to in subsection (2) being longer than the maximum benefit period calculated under subsection 10(15).
-- src:542 | Limitation
-- src:543 | (3.4) An extension under one or more of subsections 10(10) to (13.02) must not result in the period referred to in subsection (2) being longer than 104 weeks.
-- The length of the period in weeks with every extension. (3.1): the extensions of (3) and (3.01) stop at 104 weeks.
-- (3.3): an extension under (3.2) must not make the period longer than the maximum benefit period of s 10(15), which the
-- caller passes in. (3.4): no extension may make the period longer than 104 weeks. The last two are read as limits on
-- the whole period (fork F-23-3.4 in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(2), s 23(3.1), s 23(3.3), s 23(3.4) (src:521) (src:525) (src:541) (src:543)
GIVEN `the weeks of extension under subsection (3)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.01)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.2)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.21)` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.22)` IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum number of weeks in the benefit period calculated under subsection 10(15)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(2) to (3.4) the length of the period in weeks` IS
    min 104 (`the length after the extension under subsection (3.2)` PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.21)` PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.22)`)
    WHERE
        `the length after the extensions under subsections (3) and (3.01)` MEANS
            min `s 23(3.1) the longest the period may be after an extension under subsection (3) or (3.01), in weeks`
                (52 PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (3)` PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.01)`)
        `the length after the extension under subsection (3.2)` MEANS
            IF `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.2)` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN max `the length after the extensions under subsections (3) and (3.01)`
                     (min (`the length after the extensions under subsections (3) and (3.01)` PLUS `the weeks of extension under subsection (3.2)`)
                          `the maximum number of weeks in the benefit period calculated under subsection 10(15)`)
            ELSE `the length after the extensions under subsections (3) and (3.01)`

-- src:545 | (3.5) If benefits are payable to a claimant for the reasons set out in this section and any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for the same reasons under a provincial law, the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act are to be reduced or eliminated as prescribed.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(3.5) (src:545)
GIVEN `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for the same reasons under a provincial law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act` IS A NUMBER
      -- out of range: regs 76.16 and 76.17 (piece er4)
      `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(3.5) the benefits payable to the claimant after the reduction for allowances payable under a provincial law` IS
    IF `benefits are payable to the claimant for the reasons set out in section 23`
       AND `any allowances, money or other benefits are payable to the claimant for the same reasons under a provincial law`
    THEN max 0 (`the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act` MINUS `the amount by which the regulations reduce the benefits`)
    ELSE `the benefits payable to the claimant under this Act`

§ `Section 23(4) to (4.11) - dividing the weeks between the claimants`

-- src:549 | (4.1) For greater certainty, if, in respect of the same child or children, a major attachment claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and an individual makes a claim for benefits under section 152.05, the total number of weeks of benefits payable under this section and section 152.05 that may be divided between them may not exceed
-- src:550 | (a) 40, if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection (1.1) or 152.05(1.1) is established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) or 152.14(1)(b)(i); or
-- src:551 | (b) 69, if that number of weeks is established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) or 152.14(1)(b)(ii).
-- The total that may be divided between two claimants for the same child or children: 40 weeks for the 35-week election,
-- 69 for the 61-week election (subsection (4), repeated "for greater certainty" in (4.1)).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(4), s 23(4.1) (src:547) (src:549-551)
GIVEN election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(4) and s 23(4.1) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` IS
    IF election EQUALS `the 35-week maximum` THEN 40 ELSE 69

-- src:553 | (4.11) Even if the weeks of benefits payable are divided in accordance with subsections (4) and (4.1), the maximum number of weeks for which benefits may be paid to a claimant is 35 or 61 weeks, in accordance with the election made under subsection (1.1) or 152.05(1.1).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(4.11) (src:553)
GIVEN election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 23(4.11) the most weeks of benefits that may be paid to one claimant` IS
    IF election EQUALS `the 35-week maximum` THEN 35 ELSE 61

-- src:547 | (4) If two major attachment claimants each make a claim for benefits under this section — or if one major attachment claimant makes a claim for benefits under this section and an individual makes a claim for benefits under section 152.05 — in respect of the same child or children, the weeks of benefits payable under this section, under section 152.05 or under both those sections may be divided between them up to a maximum of 40, if the maximum number of weeks that has been elected under subsection (1.1) or 152.05(1.1) is established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(i) or 152.14(1)(b)(i), or up to a maximum of 69, if that number of weeks is established under subparagraph 12(3)(b)(ii) or 152.14(1)(b)(ii). If they cannot agree, the weeks of benefits are to be divided in accordance with the prescribed rules.
-- The claimants may divide the weeks "up to a maximum" (the total) and neither may be paid more than their own maximum.
-- If they cannot agree, the weeks are divided "in accordance with the prescribed rules" (reg 41.6, piece er3).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(4) (src:547)
GIVEN election IS AN `Election of maximum weeks`
      `the weeks of benefits divided to the first claimant` IS A NUMBER
      `the weeks of benefits divided to the second claimant` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(4) the division of the weeks of benefits between the claimants is within the limits` IF
        `the weeks of benefits divided to the first claimant` PLUS `the weeks of benefits divided to the second claimant` AT MOST `s 23(4) and s 23(4.1) the most weeks of benefits that may be divided between the claimants` election
    AND `the weeks of benefits divided to the first claimant` AT MOST `s 23(4.11) the most weeks of benefits that may be paid to one claimant` election
    AND `the weeks of benefits divided to the second claimant` AT MOST `s 23(4.11) the most weeks of benefits that may be paid to one claimant` election

@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(4) (src:547)
GIVEN `the claimants agree on a division of the weeks of benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(4) the weeks of benefits are divided in accordance with the prescribed rules` IF
    NOT (`the claimants agree on a division of the weeks of benefits`)

§ `Section 23(5) and 23(6) - deferring the waiting period`

-- src:555 | (5) A major attachment claimant who makes a claim for benefits under this section may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period, otherwise than under section 22 or this section, if
-- src:556 | (a) the claimant has already made a claim for benefits under section 22 or this section in respect of the same child and has served the waiting period;
-- src:557 | (b) another major attachment claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 22 or this section in respect of the same child and that other claimant has served or is serving their waiting period;
-- src:558 | (c) another major attachment claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 22 or this section in respect of the same child at the same time as the claimant and that other claimant elects to serve the waiting period; or
-- src:559 | (d) the claimant or another major attachment claimant meets the prescribed requirements.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(5) (src:555-559)
GIVEN `the claimant is a major attachment claimant who makes a claim for benefits under section 23` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claimant has already made a claim for benefits under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child and has served the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another major attachment claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child and has served or is serving their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another major attachment claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      -- out of range: the prescribed requirements (no regulation in the deposited text names any)
      `the claimant or another major attachment claimant meets the prescribed requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 23(5) the claimant may have their waiting period deferred until they make another claim for benefits in the same benefit period` IF
        `the claimant is a major attachment claimant who makes a claim for benefits under section 23`
    AND (   `the claimant has already made a claim for benefits under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child and has served the waiting period`
         OR `another major attachment claimant has made a claim for benefits under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child and has served or is serving their waiting period`
         OR `another major attachment claimant is making a claim for benefits under section 22 or section 23 in respect of the same child at the same time and elects to serve the waiting period`
         OR `the claimant or another major attachment claimant meets the prescribed requirements`)

-- What subsection (6) leaves a major attachment claimant with when an individual claims under section 152.04 or 152.05 for the
-- same child or children.
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(6) (src:561-563)
DECLARE `ei1 Position of the waiting period under subsection 23(6)` IS ONE OF
    `ei1 the major attachment claimant is not required to serve a waiting period`
    `ei1 the individual may have their waiting period deferred in accordance with section 152.05`
    `ei1 subsection 23(6) does not apply`

-- src:561 | (6) If a major attachment claimant makes a claim under section 22 or this section and an individual makes a claim under section 152.04 or 152.05 in respect of the same child or children and one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period, then
-- src:562 | (a) if the major attachment claimant is not the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period, that claimant is not required to serve a waiting period; or
-- src:563 | (b) if the individual is not the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period, that claimant may have his or her waiting period deferred in accordance with section 152.05.
-- Paragraph (b) says "that claimant" may have "his or her" waiting period deferred "in accordance with section 152.05":
-- read as the individual, who is the person section 152.05 governs (fork F-23-6 in NOTES.md).
@ref Employment Insurance Act s 23(6) (src:561-563)
GIVEN `a major attachment claimant makes a claim under section 22 or section 23 and an individual makes a claim under section 152.04 or 152.05 in respect of the same child or children` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the major attachment claimant is the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `ei1 Position of the waiting period under subsection 23(6)`
DECIDE `s 23(6) the position of the waiting period when a major attachment claimant and an individual claim for the same child` IS
    BRANCH IF NOT (`a major attachment claimant makes a claim under section 22 or section 23 and an individual makes a claim under section 152.04 or 152.05 in respect of the same child or children` AND `one of them has served or elected to serve their waiting period`)
              THEN `ei1 subsection 23(6) does not apply`
           IF `the major attachment claimant is the one who served or elected to serve the waiting period`
              THEN `ei1 the individual may have their waiting period deferred in accordance with section 152.05`
           OTHERWISE `ei1 the major attachment claimant is not required to serve a waiting period`
